kly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to discuss other candidates. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's ability to make correct decisions quickly is a direct evidence of decision quality, which is crucial, and his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation, despite communication difficulty. Compare with B's lack of direct decision-making evidence. Also note C's excellent attention skills. However C's egocentric and not willing to further education may be concerns.\n\nAlternatively, Candidate D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate A has leadership but unfriendly and unhealthy habits may affect reliability.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate is strongest overall. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's direct decision-making ability and attention skills outweigh B's indirect inference, and his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation, while his communication difficulty is a concern but may be mitigated.\n\nWe need to reference the discussion: we can say \"While Agent 1 highlighted B's reliability and stress handling, we lack direct evidence of decision quality, whereas Candidate C has explicit evidence of quick correct decisions, which is vital for safety.\" Then we can propose shifting vote to C, or at least suggest reconsideration.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: Candidate C can make correct decisions quickly; puts concern for others above everything; excellent attention skills. Also mention difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric as concerns.\n\nThus we can say we currently recommend Candidate C, pending further info on teamwork.\n\nLet's produce public message: state recommendation for Candidate C, reference Agent 1's points, bring evidence, explain why C may be better.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
